              "image_path": "images/page_5_table_1.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Expression</td><td>Expression as the sum of its terms</td><td>Terms</td></tr><tr><td>13 - 2 + 6</td><td>13 + - 2 + 6</td><td>13, - 2, 6</td></tr><tr><td>5 + 6 × 3</td><td>5 + 6 × 3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>4 + 15 - 9</td><td>+ +</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>23 - 2 × 4 + 16</td><td>+ +</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>28 + 19 - 8</td><td>+ +</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.369,
            0.848,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "operations to find the value of an expression."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.406,
            0.848,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We will start with expressions having only additions (with all the subtractions suitably converted into additions)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.452,
            0.848,
            0.49
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Does changing the order in which the terms are added give different values?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.51,
            0.452,
            0.533
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Swapping and Grouping"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.542,
            0.739,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us consider a simple expression having only two terms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.57,
            0.847,
            0.628
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 6:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Madhu is flying a drone from a terrace. The drone goes 6 m up and then 4 m down. Write an expression to show how high the final position of the drone is from the terrace."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.633,
            0.846,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The drone is 6 – 4 = 2 m above the terrace. Writing it as sum of terms:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.353,
            0.659,
            0.641,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.353,
                0.659,
                0.641,
                0.701
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.709,
            0.604,
            0.729
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Will the sum change if we swap the terms?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.356,
            0.735,
            0.641,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.356,
                0.735,
                0.641,
                0.778
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.786,
            0.394,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It doesn’t in this case."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.805,
            0.847,
            0.842
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We already know that swapping the terms does not change the sum when both the terms are positive numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.851,
            0.848,
            0.891
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Will this also hold when there are terms having negative numbers as well? Take some more expressions and check."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
